{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Adopt Spring Boot 3.x as the runtime foundation for the new ModuleRunner (replacing the legacy xd-container) to align with Spring Framework 6.0 and Java 17+ requirements.",
    "Implement U1 by building a Spring Data repository abstraction on top of a Kafka compacted changelog topic, using an off-heap key-value store (e.g., Chronicle Map or MapDB) to achieve local data affinity for stateful stream processing.",
    "Design U2 and U3 around a message-acknowledgement callback hook exposed by the module-producer; offsets and state stores are checkpointed/flushed only after a successful ack, providing reliable at-least-once semantics.",
    "Implement U4 (CoAP source) as a new module using a mature CoAP client library (e.g., Californium/Eclipse), integrated with the existing source module SPI so it is pluggable like other XD/SCDF source modules.",
    "Implement U6 by extending the Sqoop job launcher to support Kerberos-secured HDFS (Kerberos authentication, secured Hadoop configuration, and principal/keytab handling).",
    "Implement U7 by generating a typed Java client around the Diego receptor REST API, integrated with the existing deployer/agent SPI.",
    "Treat U5 as documentation only: produce reference docs describing the canonical properties-file deployment manifest format with examples.",
    "Use a unified integration test harness (Testcontainers for Kafka, ZooKeeper, HDFS, CoAP) for E2E verification across U1–U8."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The increment targets an existing Spring XD / Spring Cloud Data Flow style codebase; the estimates include both new code and necessary integration glue but assume the surrounding framework (module SPI, deployer, message bus abstraction) is already in place and stable.",
    "The developer is a single, experienced Java/Spring engineer familiar with Kafka, Spring Data, and stream-processing concepts; no onboarding or learning curve is included.",
    "Unit tests and basic integration tests are included within each feature activity; a separate E2E/integration pass is budgeted as Activity A10.",
    "Existing Spring XD modules and their tests can be reused as templates (saving time) for the new CoAP source (U4) and Boot-based ModuleRunner (U8).",
    "No upstream API changes are required from external projects (Kafka brokers, Diego receptor, HDFS, CoAP peers) — all changes are client/embedder-side.",
    "The 'remaining deployment properties work' called out in U8's scope is limited to completing the property mappings and externalized configuration for the Boot-based runtime; it does not include building a new configuration server.",
    "All estimates are most-likely (single-point) work-hours; they do not include project management overhead, code review cycles beyond self-review, or release/ops activities."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and architecture/design",
      "activity_description": "Review all 8 user stories, clarify interfaces, design the off-heap store adapter, ack-based flush protocol, CoAP module SPI, and Boot-based runtime topology. Produce a short design note covering the integration points and module SPI changes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Kafka changelog Spring Data repository with off-heap affinity",
      "activity_description": "Implement a Spring Data repository implementation backed by a Kafka compacted changelog topic. Integrate an off-heap key-value store (Chronicle Map / MapDB) for local data affinity. Provide repository factory, serializer, and changelog consumer that materializes state off-heap. Includes unit and integration tests against an embedded/ Testcontainers Kafka broker.",
      "most_likely_effort": 64
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Intelligent offset flushing based on producer acks",
      "activity_description": "Hook into the module-producer acknowledgement callback to persist Kafka consumer offsets only after successful message ack. Add configuration, transactional offset commit path, and tests covering ack-success and ack-failure scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Intelligent state flushing based on producer acks",
      "activity_description": "Mirror U2 for the state store: flush/checkpoint the off-heap state store only on successful producer ack. Add a state-flush callback, batched/async flush options, and tests verifying no partial state is persisted on failure.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U4 - CoAP source module",
      "activity_description": "Create a new CoAP source module: define the module options (host, port, resources, observe mode), use a CoAP client library to subscribe to resources, and emit received messages on the message bus. Includes unit tests and an integration test using a Californium-based test server.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Documentation for properties file deployment manifest",
      "activity_description": "Author reference documentation describing the canonical properties-file deployment manifest: structure, supported keys per module type, examples for stream/job definitions, and migration notes. No code changes other than minor example fixes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Secured HDFS support for Sqoop jobs",
      "activity_description": "Extend the Sqoop job runner to authenticate against a Kerberos-secured HDFS cluster. Add Hadoop security configuration loading, principal/keytab handling, and ticket renewal. Includes tests using a Kerberized MiniHDFS / Testcontainers setup.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Java receptor client for Diego runtime",
      "activity_description": "Build a Java client around the Diego receptor REST API (task lifecycle, delegate, cancel). Provide a typed API, REST template/wiremock-based tests, and integration into the deployer abstraction so modules can be launched against Diego without xd-containers.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Boot-based ModuleRunner for container-managed environments",
      "activity_description": "Create a Spring Boot-based ModuleRunner that can host XD modules in a container-managed (e.g., Diego/Kubernetes) environment, replacing xd-containers. Includes Boot auto-configuration, module discovery, deployment property binding, lifecycle management, and tests covering single- and multi-module deployments.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "End-to-end integration testing",
      "activity_description": "Cross-feature integration pass: bring up Kafka, ZooKeeper, HDFS (Kerberized), CoAP test server, and Diego receptor mocks; run combined stream/job scenarios that exercise the changelog repository, ack-based flushing, CoAP source, Sqoop-on-secured-HDFS, and the Boot-based ModuleRunner. Includes fixing regressions found.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "U8 scope - complete remaining deployment properties work",
      "activity_description": "Finish the deployment properties work flagged in U8's scope: complete externalized configuration property mappings for the Boot-based runtime, ensure all module options are bindable via the properties file, add validation, and update sample manifests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 308
  }
}
```

